    answer: "DTF means direct to film. Artwork is produced on a transfer film and applied to the garment with heat, making it useful for colorful designs and a broad range of compatible apparel."
  - question: "Can DTF be used on dark work shirts?"
    answer: "Yes. DTF can produce bright, opaque artwork on many dark garments. The exact result depends on the fabric, artwork, and shirt selected."
  - question: "Can every employee have the same logo but a different size?"
    answer: "Yes. A crew order can include multiple garment sizes while keeping the core artwork and placement consistent. Provide an accurate size count when requesting a quote."
  - question: "How should DTF work shirts be cared for?"
